An Iranian cargo vessel was struck off Qeshm Island in the Strait of Hormuz on Sunday, killing one person and wounding four, Iranian state media said. Tehran blamed a “terrorist enemy” for the attack, which came as threats to shipping intensified around the Hormuz and Bab el-Mandeb straits.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13aed686-69f7-11f1-b0c8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26108447320171.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13aed686-69f7-11f1-b0c8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26108447320171.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a2bb4c88-afe3-11f1-9658-cfa5308d7787</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 02:35:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13aed686-69f7-11f1-b0c8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26108447320171.jpg">© Asghar Besharati, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US hosts G20 energy talks in Texas as Iran war disrupts global fuel markets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-g20-energy-talks-iran-war</link><description>
The United States begins G20 meetings in Houston on Monday promoting “energy abundance,” as President Donald Trump’s war against Iran disrupts global fuel markets. Delegations from major economies, including China, India, Japan and Germany, will attend alongside oil producers Canada and Saudi Arabia. Russia is also expected to participate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/481134d6-a5bc-11f1-b352-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/58a2a20e7d0248e924993791c7981e68d2924bcc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/481134d6-a5bc-11f1-b352-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/58a2a20e7d0248e924993791c7981e68d2924bcc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f4b68e0-afd2-11f1-90c1-3126f5b87fe4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:42:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/481134d6-a5bc-11f1-b352-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/58a2a20e7d0248e924993791c7981e68d2924bcc.jpg">© Allison Joyce, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Zverev beats Shelton to win US Open 2026 and second Grand Slam title</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260913-alexander-zverev-ben-shelton-us-open-final-tennis</link><description>
Alexander Zverev beat American Ben Shelton 6-3, 7-6 (7/2), 5-7, 6-2 on Sunday to win the US Open and claim his second Grand Slam title. The German, who lost the 2020 final, denied Shelton the chance to become the first American man to win a major since 2003.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d31c012-afc0-11f1-9bdc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/fe95c88ec2abe893e783e406aac9db91260241b5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d31c012-afc0-11f1-9bdc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/fe95c88ec2abe893e783e406aac9db91260241b5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2162f8a0-afc2-11f1-94c2-190219c58545</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:39:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d31c012-afc0-11f1-9bdc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/fe95c88ec2abe893e783e406aac9db91260241b5.jpg">© ANGELA WEISS, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>The 'authenticity' of Celine Dion: 'She appeals to the Boomers and the Zoomers'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-the-authenticity-of-celine-dion-she-appeals-to-the-boomers-and-the-zoomers</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Nick Rees-Roberts, Professor of Media, Culture and Communication at the Sorbonne Nouvelle University, Paris. According to Roberts, Celine Dion’s extraordinary return to Paris reveals something larger than the enduring popularity of a global pop star. Her appeal lies in an unusual ability to bridge categories that contemporary celebrity and pop culture often keep separate: generations, languages, cultural hierarchies and even the apparent opposition between authenticity and carefully constructed stardom.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f6ad15e-afb7-11f1-b6e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15789222536aa71114598923-15969308.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6f6ad15e-afb7-11f1-b6e0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15789222536aa71114598923-15969308.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8c2d3862-afb8-11f1-9c69-9b5a26ca6f48</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:18:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Sweden Election Aftermath: A hard night for the hard right?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sweden-election-aftermath-a-hard-night-for-the-hard-right</link><description>
Immediate France 24 analysis as polls close, and exit polls indicate how the country has voted in the 2026 election.
 
France 24 Gavin Lee has been speaking to Scandinavia Correspondent Trine Villeman
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">968803b4-afa4-11f1-a9ff-7b8ae3515f31</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:04:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Sucker Punch: How the Houthis shocked the Gulf</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-sucker-punch-how-the-houthis-shocked-the-gulf</link><description><![CDATA[
Who are the Houthis, what are their objectives for Yemen, and could the Iranian backed group how a significant chunk of world trade to ransom in the Bab el Mandeb Strait?
 
Professor Thomas Juneau, a specialist on the Houthis & Iran, explains the intricate dynamics about the group, it’s repressive nature and the level of the threat to world shipping. He’s been speaking to France 24’s Gavin Lee
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da10a4d0-af98-11f1-baf1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/BMAJKTF755OODMUOC5K2B5WLAA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da10a4d0-af98-11f1-baf1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/BMAJKTF755OODMUOC5K2B5WLAA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb25fec0-af9f-11f1-96a9-f90414a18a16</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:46:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Sweden's centre-left holds razor-thin edge as exit polls show tight race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-leads-election-as-far-right-slips-exit-polls-show</link><description>
Sweden's general election remained too close to call early Monday, with nearly 90% of votes counted. Four opposition parties led by Social Democrat Magdalena Andersson held a one-seat parliamentary lead over Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson's right-wing bloc, which includes the Sweden Democrats, as both leaders said they were ready to govern.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6a890ec-af9e-11f1-80aa-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T175249Z-1939019679-RC2HINAXGOPT-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6a890ec-af9e-11f1-80aa-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T175249Z-1939019679-RC2HINAXGOPT-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3da4af80-afa0-11f1-aa6e-1122ecf5d05d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:25:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6a890ec-af9e-11f1-80aa-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T175249Z-1939019679-RC2HINAXGOPT-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg">© Denis Balibouse, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine, Poland condemn Russia after drone strikes train near border</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-poland-ukraine-slam-russian-strikes-near-border-as-escalation</link><description>
Ukraine and Poland on Sunday condemned Russian strikes close to the Polish border as an "escalation" in the war, after drones struck a Warsaw-bound train. Ukraine's rail operator said former British PM Boris Johnson and ex-US CIA director David Petraeus were at a border train station nearby around the time the train was hit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4663a8c-afaa-11f1-a871-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8868T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4663a8c-afaa-11f1-a871-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8868T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d313a32c-af9c-11f1-8fa6-8db889befaf6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:59:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4663a8c-afaa-11f1-a871-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8868T3.jpg">© Ukrainian State Emergency Service via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘I gave up my life to care for my father’: How 9/11 shaped a son’s sense of duty and life trajectory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/i-gave-up-my-life-to-care-for-my-father-how-9-11-shaped-a-son-s-sense-of-duty-and-life-trajectory</link><description>
Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Alessandro Stravato, a witness to the attacks of September 11th. His testimony offers a deeply personal account. He witnessed firsthand the second plane strike the World Trade Center from Arthur Ashe Stadium. Stravato’s first instinct was not to interpret the historical significance, just find his father, who was working at City Hall.  He found him alive, covered in debris and soot, trekking dozens of blocks through Manhattan. And while his father did survive, his health seriously deteriorated over the years. By 2015, as Alessandro's dad was losing his battle with cancer, he told his son to "stay strong."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1750c66-af8b-11f1-a643-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-225957-230927-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1750c66-af8b-11f1-a643-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-225957-230927-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6b28db6-af8b-11f1-a769-238242ee63f1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:10:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>US beats spirited France to win 12th women's basketball World Cup</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260913-us-beats-spirited-france-to-win-12th-women-s-basketball-world-cup</link><description>
The United States defeated a spirited France 97-79 in the 12th women's basketball World Cup final in Berlin on Sunday, winning for a record-extending 12th time. Playing in their first ever World Cup final, France lost their composure as the Americans turned on the afterburners in the second half.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fb8c458-afae-11f1-a62e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/d3d86332e0c7e4d02581e152e2a4541cd19b56a9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fb8c458-afae-11f1-a62e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/d3d86332e0c7e4d02581e152e2a4541cd19b56a9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ff2bd3c-af90-11f1-adc7-b92198d29e3b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:29:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6fb8c458-afae-11f1-a62e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/d3d86332e0c7e4d02581e152e2a4541cd19b56a9.jpg">© Odd ANDERSEN / AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘We did what we had to do’: 25 years on, 9/11 first responder reflects on duty, survival and family</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/we-did-what-we-had-to-do-25-years-on-9-11-first-responder-reflects-on-duty-survival-and-family</link><description>
Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome LaZetta Duncan, Retired NYPD Detective, 9/11 First Responder. Duncan remembers Ground Zero not as a historical event frozen in time, but as living history whose consequences continue to unfold and evolve 25 years on. Her testimony traces a striking progression: from the confusion and urgency of the attacks, rescue and recovery, to the grim transformation of gathering human remains and evidence inside a burning toxic apocalyptic crime scene. And we now learn of the overwhelming health consequences borne by responders despite repeated assurances that the air quality posed no health threat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202b85fe-af88-11f1-acf1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-212958-214148-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202b85fe-af88-11f1-acf1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260911-212958-214148-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2562fb24-af88-11f1-9a33-1d982ffe8823</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:18:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden: Tight election puts all eyes on the far right</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-tight-election-puts-all-eyes-on-the-far-right</link><description>
Swedes are voting in a closely fought general election that could see the far-right Sweden Democrats enter government for the first time. With immigration, crime and the economy dominating the campaign, Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson and Social Democrat leader Magdalena Andersson are locked in a neck-and-neck race.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ebf82fc-af89-11f1-86a8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-171154-171339-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ebf82fc-af89-11f1-86a8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-171154-171339-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a3efd90c-af89-11f1-848c-1d982ffe8823</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:55:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>AI : 'We need to take the risk seriously and have more coordination'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ai-we-need-to-take-the-risk-seriously-and-have-more-coordination</link><description>
This week's debate over AI has put the spotlight on how seriously we should take the technology's growing risks. On FRANCE 24, University of Salford Chair in Science Communication and Future Media, Andy Miah, argued that while AI poses real challenges requiring closer coordination between companies and governments, there is no existential threat to humanity. He also said clearer data and concrete figures would help the public better understand the risks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ae58134-af88-11f1-a801-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-170106-170725-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ae58134-af88-11f1-a801-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-170106-170725-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2feef3fe-af88-11f1-ac4c-238242ee63f1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:50:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France's far-right Marine Le Pen kicks off 2027 presidential campaign</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-far-right-marine-le-pen-kicks-off-2027-presidential-campaign</link><description>
In France, Marine Le Pen has launched her presidential campaign with a rally in Hénin-Beaumont this Sunday, despite wearing an electronic tag following her recent conviction. On FRANCE 24, international affairs editor Oliver Farry explains why she remains the frontrunner in the polls despite her weakened legal position, pointing to her long-standing national profile, the appeal of her "national preference" agenda, and the left's struggle to unite behind a convincing candidate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84518dfc-a52a-11f1-984c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T154621Z-1088021487-RC237NAUVKIC-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84518dfc-a52a-11f1-984c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T154621Z-1088021487-RC237NAUVKIC-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5cfd9510-af85-11f1-9906-179448e49bbe</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:41:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>The race to make AI safer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/the-race-to-make-ai-safer</link><description>
As AI leaders warn that the technology is advancing faster than our ability to control it, Donald Trump has dismissed some of those concerns as exaggerated. On FRANCE 24, AI philosophy professor Raphaël Millière said this summer's real-world AI security incident shows the risks are no longer hypothetical, while stressing that it does not mean "AI will kill us all". Instead, he argues the priority is coordinated action by companies and governments to manage increasingly real safety risks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a83147c-8609-11f1-9e88-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/WhatsApp-Image-2026-07-22-at-2-01-15-PM.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a83147c-8609-11f1-9e88-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/WhatsApp-Image-2026-07-22-at-2-01-15-PM.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b129e3a-af84-11f1-8f7b-8bfa1dec8c08</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:16:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Surfing: France tests Olympic venue ahead of LA 2028</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/surfing-france-tests-olympic-venue-ahead-of-la-2028</link><description>
With the Lexus Trestles Pro underway in California, the French surfing team is using the future Los Angeles 2028 Olympic venue for its first full-scale training camp. Led by reigning Olympic champion Kauli Vaast, the squad is testing both its sporting preparation and team logistics as it builds towards defending France's medal success from Paris 2024.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54130b38-af7b-11f1-8094-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-151323-151520-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54130b38-af7b-11f1-8094-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-151323-151520-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58c18f2e-af7b-11f1-9eec-f1e7b94aa4dd</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:04:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen: The Houthis test Iran's regional influence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-yemen-the-houthis-test-iran-s-regional-influence</link><description>
Iran-backed Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia have intensified as fighting spreads around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a vital chokepoint for global trade and oil shipments. On FRANCE 24, Sanaa Center for Strategic Studies chairman Farea Al-Muslimi argued this could mark "the last round in Yemen's current war", unpacking the Houthis' ties with Iran and the growing pressure on Washington as the group targets US allies while Donald Trump heads into a crucial election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e97ed2ba-adc3-11f1-b34d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253315512845.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e97ed2ba-adc3-11f1-b34d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253315512845.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a9a1ea8-af74-11f1-9ade-8d251d540f38</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:29:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Indonesia: Second ferry disaster in five days</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days</link><description>
At least one person has died and more than 100 people remain missing after a ferry carrying 243 people sank in rough weather between the Indonesian islands of Java and Borneo. The disaster is the second major ferry accident in the region in five days, renewing concerns over safety standards, overcrowding and maintenance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2167cbc-af62-11f1-84e0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-121016-121213-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2167cbc-af62-11f1-84e0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-121016-121213-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e6e73e0c-af62-11f1-a370-6ba72121faf5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:17:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen: Fighting escalates around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait</link><description>
Fighting is escalating in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi forces seized strategic territory around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, prompting counterstrikes by government forces and reported Saudi air raids. The Houthis also claimed attacks inside southern Saudi Arabia and threatened to disrupt shipping through the key maritime chokepoint, raising fears for regional security and global trade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abc04a1a-af6e-11f1-819a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-140115-140311-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abc04a1a-af6e-11f1-819a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-140115-140311-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b0d9495c-af6e-11f1-acd2-8d251d540f38</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:15:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Swedish far-right eyes role in government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government</link><description>
As Sweden heads into a closely fought election, the far right is gaining ground by tapping into concerns over crime and security, issues that some voters increasingly associate with migration. On FRANCE 24, Stockholm University sociologist Zeth Isaksson said the movement has also softened its image in recent years, making it more acceptable to a broader electorate, while also cautioning against overstating the strength of the far right in Sweden.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d325c64-af53-11f1-8d54-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20799631186aa669301c83e0-07656090.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d325c64-af53-11f1-8d54-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20799631186aa669301c83e0-07656090.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9efc97ae-af71-11f1-a226-7db7cf189a1f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:11:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Radio France staff strike over appointment of far-right weekly editor</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-radio-france-staff-strike-over-appointment-of-far-right-weekly-editor</link><description>
Staff at public broadcaster Radio France began a two-day strike on Sunday over the appointment of Charles Sapin, deputy editor-in-chief at far-right weekly Valeurs Actuelles. Unions accuse Sapin of promoting far-right ideas ahead of next spring's presidential election, while management has defended the appointment in the name of pluralism.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02d53bbe-af04-11f1-9d7b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e1d9fdbe2d48d1241c3b6d21d639c8533611857e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02d53bbe-af04-11f1-9d7b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e1d9fdbe2d48d1241c3b6d21d639c8533611857e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ef9108e-af70-11f1-8f8f-7db7cf189a1f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:44:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02d53bbe-af04-11f1-9d7b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e1d9fdbe2d48d1241c3b6d21d639c8533611857e.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: Michelle Bolsonaro's key role in the presidential race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race</link><description>
Brazil is heading to the polls on October 4, with President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva seeking a fourth term as the Bolsonaro family mounts a political comeback through Flávio's presidential bid and Michelle's Senate campaign. With polls pointing to another tight race, Michelle's popularity among women could prove crucial as the family tries to return to power.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ece2006-af62-11f1-9504-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-120821-121000-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ece2006-af62-11f1-9504-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-120821-121000-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83e41de8-af62-11f1-a945-0121a29fa1cc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:08:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>The week in pictures: 9/11 anniversary, far-right win in Germany and Houthis' Yemen offensive</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive</link><description>
